From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:05:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media (ohos): Prepare the player of an audio element

The OpenHarmony AVPlayer backend only prepared a player once the window
of its video output was set, and only video elements have one, so an
audio element never got past HAVE_NOTHING, and its play() promise never
settled. Prepare a player without video output as soon as AVPlayer is
initialized.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: Every WPT test that plays an audio element hung on OpenHarmony
before; see Validation.

Validation: a HiHope DAYU200 (OpenHarmony 7.0, API 26), headless release builds (`./mach build --ohos --headless-binary`) of ohos-main with and without this patch, with and without patches 68 to 71. A direct check: audio elements with sound_0.oga, sound_0.mp3 and test-1s.mp4 now load, play and end (before: readyState 0, no error, play() pending forever); video elements are unchanged. `./mach test-wpt --ohos --processes 2` of the series' ten media tests (gc-unreferenced-media-element, ended-current-playback-position, preload-none-play, allowed-to-play, autoplay, resource-selection-candidate-moved, the three autoplay permissions policy tests, played-loop): without this patch every test with an audio element hangs; with it and patches 68 to 71, all pass with SpiderMonkey and QuickJS except resource-selection-candidate-moved, which hangs until the next patch connects the AVPlayer error callback, and autoplay-default-permissions-policy, which is OK against its TIMEOUT expectation as on Linux on this host. One QuickJS run hung in autoplay.html, possibly from the H.264 decoder limit that the next patch describes; it passed 3 of 3 in isolation with each engine. With this patch but without patches 68 to 71, the GC test and preload-none-play fail with SpiderMonkey, and with QuickJS the tests time out as on Linux before the series.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; root-caused, written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .../backends/ohos/ohos_media/avplayer.rs      | 24 ++++++++++++-------
 components/media/backends/ohos/player.rs      |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/media/backends/ohos/ohos_media/avplayer.rs b/components/media/backends/ohos/ohos_media/avplayer.rs
index d2958132323..d24da572d55 100644
--- a/components/media/backends/ohos/ohos_media/avplayer.rs
+++ b/components/media/backends/ohos/ohos_media/avplayer.rs
@@ -54,14 +54,16 @@ pub struct OhosPlayer {
     frame_available_callback_closure: Option<*mut Box<dyn Fn()>>,
     native_window: Option<*mut OHNativeWindow>,
     has_set_source_size: bool,
-    has_set_window: bool,
+    /// Whether the player renders video, in which case it only prepares once its window is set.
+    has_video_output: bool,
+    has_prepared: bool,
     volume: f64,
     playback_rate: f64,
     state: AVPlayerState,
 }
 
 impl OhosPlayer {
-    pub fn new() -> Self {
+    pub fn new(has_video_output: bool) -> Self {
         debug!("Creating OHOS Player!");
         OhosPlayer {
             native_image: None,
@@ -71,7 +73,8 @@ impl OhosPlayer {
             frame_available_callback_closure: None,
             native_window: None,
             has_set_source_size: false,
-            has_set_window: false,
+            has_video_output,
+            has_prepared: false,
             volume: 1.0,
             playback_rate: 1.0,
             state: AVPlayerState::AV_IDLE,
@@ -90,14 +93,17 @@ impl OhosPlayer {
     /// 2. after running external initialize step.
     ///    e.g. setup_window_buffer_listener
     pub fn initialize_check_state_action(&mut self) {
-        if self.state == AVPlayerState::AV_INITIALIZED &&
-            self.native_window.is_some() &&
-            !self.has_set_window
-        {
-            self.has_set_window = true;
+        if self.state != AVPlayerState::AV_INITIALIZED || self.has_prepared {
+            return;
+        }
+        if self.has_video_output {
+            if self.native_window.is_none() {
+                return;
+            }
             self.set_window_to_player();
-            self.prepare(); // only prepare after setting window.
         }
+        self.has_prepared = true;
+        self.prepare(); // only prepare after setting window, if any.
     }
 
     fn set_window_to_player(&mut self) {
